# Files copied into each new worktree created by Claude Code or Codex.
#
# .gitignore syntax. Only paths that match AND are gitignored get copied, so
# tracked files are never duplicated, and a pattern that is not ignored here is
# silently skipped. These are copies, not symlinks: each worktree must work
# without touching another one.
#
# Machine-local generated state is deliberately absent. Fish variables and
# .config/fish/completions.local/ are read from $HOME through the installed
# symlinks rather than from a worktree, and .agents/memory/ holds per-task notes
# that should not be duplicated across parallel worktrees.

# Per-project tool permissions, so a fresh worktree does not re-prompt for
# everything the main checkout has already granted.
.claude/settings.local.json
